    <div class="toc"><h5>On this page</h5><div class="toc-list"><a onclick="scrollToId('p-overview')"><span>1.</span> Overview</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-does')"><span>2.</span> What FormPilot does</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-process')"><span>3.</span> Where your data is processed</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-stored')"><span>4.</span> What is stored, and where</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-notdo')"><span>5.</span> What FormPilot does not do</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-perms')"><span>6.</span> Permissions FormPilot requests</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-thirdparty')"><span>7.</span> Third-party services</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-rights')"><span>8.</span> Your choices and controls</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-children')"><span>9.</span> Children's privacy</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-intl')"><span>10.</span> International users</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-changes')"><span>11.</span> Changes to this policy</a><a onclick="scrollToId('p-contact')"><span>12.</span> Contact</a></div></div>

    <h2 id="p-overview">1. Overview</h2>
    <p>FormPilot ("the extension," "we," "our") is a Chrome browser extension that helps you copy data from an image or PDF document and fill matching fields into a web form. This policy explains what data the extension handles, where it is processed, and what is &mdash; and is not &mdash; stored. It applies to the FormPilot browser extension and to this website.</p>

    <h2 id="p-does">2. What FormPilot does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Reads a document (image or PDF) you choose to upload, or a screenshot you choose to capture, and extracts text from it using on-device optical character recognition (OCR) and PDF parsing.</li>
      <li>Scans the form fields present on a web page &mdash; only when you click <strong>"Scan this form."</strong></li>
      <li>Fills form fields on a web page &mdash; only when you click <strong>"Fill form now."</strong></li>
      <li>Lets you right-click an image or a page to start an extraction directly, as a shortcut to the same upload flow.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="p-process">3. Where your data is processed</h2>
    <p>All document processing &mdash; OCR, PDF text extraction, and field matching &mdash; happens locally, inside your own browser, on your own device. Files you upload and screenshots you capture are <strong>never uploaded</strong> to any server operated by us or by anyone else. There is no backend server that FormPilot's core functionality depends on.</p>
    <div class="callout">The one exception: the first time you use OCR in a given language (for example, Hindi or Gujarati), the extension downloads that language's recognition data from a public, third-party host, <code>tessdata.projectnaptha.com</code>. This is a one-time download of a generic language model &mdash; it contains no information about you, your documents, or your activity, and nothing about your request is personally identifying.</div>

    <h2 id="p-stored">4. What is stored, and where</h2>
    <p>FormPilot stores two kinds of information, both locally on your device via Chrome's built-in <code>chrome.storage.local</code> API:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Confirmed field mappings</strong> &mdash; for example, "on this website, 'Customer Name' means 'Party Name'" &mdash; saved per website domain, so you don't have to re-confirm familiar matches the next time you use that site.</li>
      <li><strong>Your preferences</strong> &mdash; your chosen interface language and OCR language selection.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>None of this is transmitted to us or to any third party at any point. It stays on your device, inside your browser profile, and is only accessible to the FormPilot extension itself. You can clear it at any time via <strong>"Forget remembered fields for this site"</strong> in the extension's settings panel, or by removing the extension entirely, which deletes all locally stored data along with it.</p>

    <h2 id="p-notdo">5. What FormPilot does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Does not require an account, sign-in, or any personal information to function.</li>
      <li>Does not sell, rent, or share your data with third parties, under any circumstance.</li>
      <li>Does not use your data for advertising, profiling, or cross-site tracking.</li>
      <li>Does not transmit the content of any document, form, or web page to any server.</li>
      <li>Does not run in the background monitoring your browsing &mdash; it only acts when you click Scan or Fill.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="p-perms">6. Permissions FormPilot requests</h2>
    <p>Chrome requires an extension to declare upfront every capability it may use. Here is what each permission FormPilot requests is for, in plain terms:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>storage</code> &mdash; to save field-mapping preferences and settings locally, as described in section 4.</li>
      <li><code>scripting</code>, <code>activeTab</code>, <code>tabs</code> &mdash; to scan and fill the form in the tab you select, and to list your open tabs so you can choose one.</li>
      <li><code>contextMenus</code> &mdash; to add the right-click options "Extract data from this image" and "Extract data from this page."</li>
      <li><code>sidePanel</code> &mdash; to display the extension's interface.</li>
      <li><strong>Access to all websites</strong> &mdash; because the source document and the destination form can be on any website you choose. FormPilot only reads or modifies a page's content when you explicitly click Scan or Fill.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="p-thirdparty">7. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>FormPilot's OCR engine (Tesseract.js) and PDF engine (pdf.js) are open-source libraries that run entirely inside the extension, on your device &mdash; they are not third-party services that receive your data. The single external request FormPilot makes is the one-time OCR language-data download described in section 3. This website itself does not use third-party analytics or advertising trackers.</p>

    <h2 id="p-rights">8. Your choices and controls</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You decide which documents to upload and which forms to fill &mdash; nothing happens automatically.</li>
      <li>You can review and edit every extracted field and every suggested match before anything is filled.</li>
      <li>You can clear remembered mappings for any one website, at any time.</li>
      <li>You can uninstall the extension at any time via <code>chrome://extensions</code>, which removes all locally stored data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="p-children">9. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>FormPilot is a productivity tool intended for general, professional use (for example, by accountants and data-entry operators) and is not directed at children. It does not knowingly collect data from children, and given it collects no personal data from anyone, there is no age-gated functionality to speak of.</p>

    <h2 id="p-intl">10. International users</h2>
    <p>Because FormPilot does not transmit or store your data on any server, there is no cross-border data transfer to disclose: your information never leaves your own device, regardless of where you are located.</p>

    <h2 id="p-changes">11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted at this same URL with a revised "Last updated" date above. Material changes will also be reflected in the extension's Chrome Web Store listing.</p>

    <h2 id="p-contact">12. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy, or about how FormPilot handles data, can be sent to: <strong class="js-email">[YOUR SUPPORT EMAIL]</strong>.</p>
