<div class="page" id="page-faq">
  <section class="page-hero container">
    <span class="eyebrow"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M13 2L4 14h6l-1 8 9-12h-6l1-8z" fill="currentColor"/></svg> Support</span>
    <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
    <p>Can't find what you need? <a onclick="goPage('contact')" style="color:var(--cyan);cursor:pointer;">Get in touch</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="legal container" style="max-width:816px;">
    <div class="faq-cat">General</div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Is FormPilot free?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">Yes. Every feature currently available is free, with no account, trial limit, or credit card required. We may introduce an optional paid tier for teams later, but the features that are free today are intended to stay free.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Do I need to create an account?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">No. FormPilot works entirely without sign-in. There's nothing to register for and nothing stored about you beyond the on-device preferences described in the Privacy Policy.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">What browsers does FormPilot support?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">FormPilot is built for Google Chrome (Manifest V3) and other Chromium-based browsers that support the same extension platform, such as Microsoft Edge and Brave.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Will there be a paid version?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">Possibly, for team-oriented features like shared mappings or usage history &mdash; see the Pricing section on the home page. Nothing free today will be taken away or put behind a paywall.</div></div></div><div class="faq-cat">Using FormPilot</div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">What file types can I upload?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">Images (JPG, PNG, and similar formats) and PDF files &mdash; both scanned/image-based PDFs and PDFs with a native text layer or fillable form fields.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Which languages are supported?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">Field matching and the extension's own interface currently support English, Hindi, and Gujarati. More languages can be added to the matching dictionary over time.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Does FormPilot work on every website?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">FormPilot can scan and fill standard form fields &mdash; text inputs, dropdowns, checkboxes, radio buttons, and editable text areas &mdash; on most websites. Some heavily customized or non-standard form widgets may not be recognized.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">What happens if a field isn't matched?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">FormPilot never guesses silently. Any extracted field it can't confidently match to a destination field is clearly flagged as unmatched, so you can fill it manually or adjust the match yourself.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Can I correct a match before filling?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">Yes. Every suggested match is shown with a confidence score before anything is filled, and you can review or override it.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Can I use FormPilot on a PDF opened directly in Chrome's built-in viewer?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">FormPilot works best when you upload the PDF file directly into the side panel. Reading a PDF that's merely open in a browser tab (rather than uploaded) depends on how that page serves the file.</div></div></div><div class="faq-cat">Privacy &amp; security</div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Is my data safe?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">Yes. All processing &mdash; OCR, PDF parsing, and field matching &mdash; happens locally in your browser. Nothing is uploaded to any server. See the full Privacy Policy for details.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Does FormPilot store my documents?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">No. Documents are processed in memory while you work with them and are not retained afterward. The only thing FormPilot stores is a small record of which field labels you've confirmed match on a given website &mdash; not the documents or data themselves.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Why does FormPilot need access to all websites?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">Because the source document and destination form can be on any two unrelated websites you choose. FormPilot only reads or modifies a page when you explicitly click Scan or Fill &mdash; it does not run in the background.</div></div></div><div class="faq-cat">Troubleshooting &amp; support</div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Why didn't a field get filled correctly?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">Most often this means OCR misread a character, or the field's label was unusual enough that it fell below the matching confidence threshold. Review the extracted text and the suggested match before filling &mdash; you can always correct either one.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">How do I report a bug or request a feature?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">Use the Contact page, or reach out at the support email listed there. Specific examples (a screenshot, the website involved) help a lot.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Is FormPilot open source?<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></div><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-in">FormPilot's OCR and PDF-parsing components are built on the open-source Tesseract.js and pdf.js projects. The extension itself is not currently open source.</div></div></div>
  </div>
</div>


